    "title": "Sessions",
    "body": "With a **session**, the server stores \"session 7f2c… is Alice, until next month\" in a shared store, and the app sends only the random session ID. Every request costs one lookup: at 5,000 requests per second, about 5% of a store that handles 100,000. In return, logging out or blocking Alice deletes the session, and her **next request fails at once**.",
