  {
    "title": "Signed tokens",
    "body": "With a **token**, the server gives Alice a small signed note: \"Alice, valid until 10:15\". Any server checks the signature and the time by itself, with **no lookup**. But the note cannot be called back: if Alice is blocked at 10:00, her token still works until **10:15**. So access tokens are kept short, and a long-lived **refresh token**, checked on the server, gets new ones. A block then stops the next refresh.",
