  {
    "title": "Least privilege",
    "body": "A small reporting service reads orders for daily totals. If it connects as the database administrator, a flaw in it could **delete every order**. With **least privilege**, it has its own database user that can only read the orders table. If an attacker takes over the reporting service, the damage is limited to reading orders. The same rule applies to people, keys and tokens: give each only what it needs.",
