  {
    "title": "Limit the guessing",
    "body": "A guesser tries common passwords against Alice's account. The login service allows **5 failed attempts per account every 15 minutes**: a day has 96 such periods, so the guesser gets 5 × 96 = **480** tries a day, and a list of a million common passwords would take over 2,000 days. The wait ends by itself, so nobody can lock Alice out for good. A limit per network address helps too, but alone it fails against a guesser with many addresses.",
